  "body": "PR140 could not read selector values because the resident attribute buffer is 2,030,043,136 bytes, above its 1 GiB logical extent cap. This adds private native/host adapters admitting a 2 GiB logical buffer while retaining four raw texels per window, 64 bytes per window and 960 bytes total. The original helper and receiver remain unchanged.\n\nThe observer records RSS highwater before/after and marks an increase above 32 MiB as partial. Tests use a real read-only sparse mapping with the actual 2.03 GB extent, literal far-end/wrapped values, forbidden whole-copy paths, and bounded RSS. Coordinates, offsets, raw hashes, policy/counters, identity and inherited lifecycle/source-image gates remain independently validated. Exact -I -S -B native help passes.\n\nValidation so far: 16 new tests and 131 focused CPU regressions, plus actionlint. One independent wholebranch review and exact source CI precede one bounded native renderer replay. No local SDK/Panda/GLX/model, full-buffer copy, GPU readback, new dependencies, extra render/task/state setters, or original gate promotion. Original matrix remains 3/4 PASS, overall FAIL, Stage7=false.\n\nStacked on Draft PR140; no main merge or environment/registry publication. Actual evidence and final exact-HEAD CI will be recorded before closeout.\n",
